"""Cross-check values for Research Studio M1 methods, computed with SciPy/NumPy.

Written by the architect on 2026-09-27 (docs/research/M1-DESIGN.md section 13). These are a SECOND,
independent implementation, not the pin: the pin for every method is R 4.6.0 (tests/fixtures/r/,
generated by the rparity role) or a published source (NIST StRD, the course deck, the serosurvey
numbers checked by work/research-studio/workspace/check.py). A method's fixture test should assert
against R and against these values; a disagreement between R and SciPy beyond tolerance is a bug
report, not a choice.

Every dataset below is defined here, literally, so no value depends on recalling a published table.
Closed forms are written out where SciPy has no function, and are marked "formula".

Run:  PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8 python scipy_crosscheck.py  (writes scipy-crosscheck.json beside it)
"""
